# Shell scripts must always keep LF line endings, regardless of a
# contributor's core.autocrlf setting - a CRLF shebang line breaks exec()
# inside a Linux container ("no such file or directory" for a file that
# demonstrably exists). This matters most for services/web/docker-
# entrypoint.sh, which is COPY'd into the web image and run as ENTRYPOINT,
# but applies uniformly to every scripts/*.sh helper too, all of which are
# only ever run under bash/Git Bash on Linux-style shells.
*.sh text eol=lf
